.TH OMX-RT-GATE 1 "" "omx-dsp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
omx-rt-gate \- prove that real-time C never allocates, locks, sleeps or does I/O
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B omx-rt-gate
\fB\-\-abi\fR \fINAME\fR[\fB:host\fR]... [\fB\-\-tags\fR \fIFILE\fR]... [\fB\-\-graphs\fR \fIDIR\fR]...
[\fB\-\-list\-roots\fR] \fB\-\-\fR \fICC\fR [\fIFLAGS\fR...] \fIUNIT.c\fR...
.br
.B omx-rt-gate \-\-check\-tables
.br
.B omx-rt-gate \-\-thread\-tags
\fIOUT\fR [\fB\-\-selfrun\fR \fIUNIT.c\fR] [\fB\-\-under\fR \fIDIR\fR] \fB\-\-\fR \fICC\fR [\fIFLAGS\fR...] \fIHEADERS.c\fR
.br
.B omx-rt-gate \-\-write\-graphs
\fIDIR\fR \fB\-\-\fR \fICC\fR [\fIFLAGS\fR...] \fIUNIT.c\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
The gate reads the real-time translation units of a plugin or an engine the
way the compiler sees them. Each unit is compiled with the flags given after
\fB\-\-\fR plus \fB\-O0 \-fno\-inline \-fcallgraph\-info\fR, which writes its
call graph with every macro expanded, every static function named per unit and
every indirect call marked at its site, and is preprocessed with the same
flags. The graphs are joined by symbol name to the graphs omx-dsp ships for its
own compiled units. An optimised build is never the input: dead-code removal
takes a planted malloc out of the graph. A distribution's fortification and
stack protector are taken out as well: the one warns at \-O0, the other calls
\fB__stack_chk_fail\fR, the compiler's own guard, which no source writes.
.PP
The roots are not listed by hand. They are the functions the preprocessed unit
stores in the fields of an ABI's tables: an \fBLV2_Descriptor\fR, an
\fBLV2_Worker_Interface\fR, a \fBclap_plugin\fR, a \fBpw_filter_events\fR, by an
initializer, a compound literal or an assignment to the field. The role of
each field is declared once, in the ABI's roles file; a consumer names the ABIs
it binds with \fB\-\-abi\fR and adds none of its own.
.PP
From every root the gate follows every call. It prints one line per finding:
.PP
.RS
\fICODE\fR \fIsymbol\fR \fBat\fR \fIfile\fR:\fIline\fR:\fIcol\fR \fBvia\fR \fIroot\fR[\fIrole\fR] \fB\->\fR ...
.RE
.TP
.B RT\-ALLOC, RT\-LOCK, RT\-BLOCK, RT\-IO, RT\-LOG
a symbol of the forbidden list. A worker root (LV2 \fBwork\fR) is held to the
same list as an audio root: its time is unbounded, but it allocates nothing,
takes no lock and does no I/O or logging.
.TP
.B RT\-EXTERNAL
an external symbol the class table does not classify.
.TP
.B RT\-THREAD
an omx-dsp function tagged \fB@thread worker\fR or \fB@thread control\fR reached
from an audio root.
.TP
.B RT\-INDIRECT
an indirect call the gate cannot classify. The field read at the site must be a
role a bound ABI declares, or a vtable: the targets are the functions an
initializer or a store puts into that field, and each is walked like a direct
call.
.TP
.B RT\-ROLE
an indirect call into a worker role from an audio root.
.TP
.B RT\-RESULT
the worker's result crosses by pointer. It must cross by value: a fixed-size
type with no pointer field, copied inside the callback that delivers it (LV2
\fBwork_response\fR, by \fBmemcpy\fR into a local or by dereferencing the body),
the body pointer used at most once, as that copy's argument; or word atomics.
Work's \fBrespond\fR passes the address of a pointer-free local.
.PP
Before judging anything the gate compiles a probe with a planted malloc behind
a probe root, through the same compiler, tables and walk, and requires it to be
read red. A gate that cannot see it judges nothing.
.SH TABLES
The tables are installed under \fI/usr/share/omxdsp/rt\-gate/tables\fR and are
the only ones read: one forbidden list, one class table and the ABIs' roles
files. A tables directory holding any other list is refused.
.TP
.B forbidden.tbl
\fIsymbol code reason\fR: the forbidden list, with codes from the closed set
above.
.TP
.B classes.tbl
\fIsymbol class arm:case reason\fR: the external symbols a root may call, each
with its class from the closed set \fBmaths\fR, \fBbulk\-memory\fR,
\fBword\-atomic\fR, \fBclock\fR, \fBftz\-register\fR, \fBwake\fR, the arm that
measured it and the reason. \fBsem_post\fR is a wake, like FUTEX_WAKE: an atomic,
and a futex wake only when a waiter sleeps; \fBsem_wait\fR and
\fBsem_timedwait\fR stay forbidden. A row naming a site, a field, a file or a
function of omx-dsp, a class outside the set, a row without a reason or an arm,
a duplicate, or a row for a forbidden symbol is refused at load.
.TP
.B lv2.abi, clap.abi, pipewire.abi
the roles of each ABI: \fBplugin\fR fields the bound side provides (its roots),
\fBhost\fR fields the other side provides (callable with their role),
\fBhanded\fR parameters (LV2 work's respond) and the \fBresult\fR rows.
\fB\-\-abi lv2\fR binds the plugin side, \fB\-\-abi lv2:host\fR the host side.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-abi " NAME" "\fR[\fB:host\fR]"
An ABI the units bind: \fBlv2\fR, \fBclap\fR, \fBpipewire\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-tags " FILE"
The thread tags of a library's functions. The installed omx-dsp tags are read
by default.
.TP
.BI \-\-graphs " DIR"
The call graphs of a library's compiled units. The installed omx-dsp graphs are
read by default.
.TP
.B \-\-list\-roots
Print every derived root, its role and the field it was stored in.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-tables
Load the tables and every roles file and stop.
.TP
.BI \-\-thread\-tags " OUT"
Check that every function the headers under \fB\-\-under\fR declare carries
exactly one \fB@thread audio\fR, \fB@thread worker\fR or \fB@thread control\fR in
the comment above it (a file named with \fB\-\-except\fR is left out), write the
tags to \fIOUT\fR and, with \fB\-\-selfrun\fR, a unit that takes the address of
every tagged function (omx-dsp's own run).
.TP
.BI \-\-write\-graphs " DIR"
Compile each unit the way the gate reads one and leave its call graph,
\fIDIR/<unit>.ci\fR, for a library to ship (omx-dsp's own under
\fI/usr/share/omxdsp/rt\-gate/graphs\fR).
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 when every root was walked and nothing is red; 1 when something is red; 2
when nothing was judged: a table refused at load, a unit that does not compile,
no root, a root missing from the graphs, the positive control blind. Never a
pass in place of a judgement.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
omx-rt-gate \-\-abi lv2 \-\- gcc $(pkg-config \-\-cflags omxdsp) \-Isrc src/plugin_lv2.c
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR omx-dsp-copy-check (1)
